    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An isolating switch is a device that serves to isolate a circuit or a piece of equipment from its power supply for safe maintenance or servicing. Typically, they are designed to be operated manually when the circuit is already de-energized."
